  "note": "the loss is real and the premature flag does not move. FinalityBench sets that flag when the agent ships while the *original* capture reference is undetermined, and on these archetypes the original has already failed by the time a replacement is submitted. Shipping against an unsettled replacement is the same mistake against a different reference, and the flag does not see it -- so the cost appears in excess loss alone. Recorded here because the paper previously described this as the premature action the benchmark detects, and the benchmark does not detect it."
